NEARS-2266 QA — regression bug evidence (PRE-EXISTING, not caused by this change)
GET /api/v1/vendor/order-details?order_id=91112 returns HTTP 500 on BOTH pre-fix and post-fix bytes.

Repro (vendor demo.store@gmail.com, store 1, parcel order 91112, zero order_details rows):

  # post-fix bytes (worktree fix/NEARS-2266-vendor-order-details-pii @ eebba02b, served :8266)
  $ curl -s -o /dev/null -w "HTTP %{http_code}\n" \
      "http://127.0.0.1:8266/api/v1/vendor/order-details?order_id=91112" \
      -H "Authorization: Bearer <vendor auth_token>" -H "vendorType: owner"
  HTTP 500      body: {"message":"Something went wrong"}

  # pre-fix bytes (primary tree feat/userapp-reskin2, served :8000)
  $ curl -s -o /dev/null -w "HTTP %{http_code}\n" \
      "http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/vendor/order-details?order_id=91112" ...
  HTTP 500      body: {"message":"Something went wrong"}

Identical on both sides => independent of NEARS-2266.

Backend log (Admin/storage/logs/laravel.log, worktree, endpoint-scoped grep):

  [2026-08-16 14:32:26] production.ERROR: [FAIL] Syntax error
    {"trace_id":"30a9698248f7f7ec9f2a544bbc4d74d6",
     "correlation_id":"e3e730b4-9c56-4116-8ffc-4b12cc89391b",
     "type":"InvalidArgumentException",
     "endpoint":"/api/v1/vendor/order-details"}

NOT a silent failure — the path is logged via AppLogger/Log with a correlation id, so no
logging-contract finding.

Mechanism (as measured by the backend engineer and confirmed here):
  orders.receiver_details IS NULL on 91112
    $ mysql -u root multi_food_db -N -e \
        "SELECT id, receiver_details IS NULL FROM orders WHERE id=91112;"
      91112   1
  Order::getReceiverDetailsAttribute (Admin/app/Models/Order.php:127-140) json_decode()s that
  NULL, which leaves json_last_error() dirty. Model::toJson()'s JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR does not
  reset that global state, so JsonResponse::setData throws
  InvalidArgumentException: Syntax error.

Blast radius: every vendor order whose receiver_details is NULL/non-JSON and which reaches the
raw-model branch of VendorController::get_order_details (parcel or prescription_order=1 with
zero order_details rows).
